🚨 **BLOCKING: CRAP ratchet regression — `fixture` grew 12 → 20.5**

The Quality gate (`crap` check) fails on this PR. Reproduced locally with the pinned `crap4js` + released baseline + coverage from the instrumented suite:

```
REGRESSION  js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js::fixture: 12 -> 20.5
NEW > 8     js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js::slotFixture: 11.2
```

The `prIndex` state-aware branch added here (plus the binary-expr growth) pushed `fixture` over its baseline value. The ratchet only ever allows CRAP to **decrease** — the baseline is not editable from a PR. To fix, shrink the fixture's decision count, e.g. extract the state-aware list payload into a small named helper:

```javascript
function listPayload(opts, pr, state) {
    if (opts.prIndex) return JSON.stringify(opts.prIndex[state || 'open'] || []);
    return JSON.stringify([{ number: pr.number }]);
}
// github_list_prs: function (a) {
//     listCalls.push(a);
//     return listPayload(opts, pr, a && a.state);
// },
```

…or add direct branch coverage for the new paths. Either way `fixture` must land back at ≤ 12 (and `slotFixture` ≤ 8, see the sibling comment).

🚨 **BLOCKING: CRAP ratchet — new function `slotFixture` is 11.2, over the threshold 8**

New functions must come in at or below `CRAP_THRESHOLD: 8` (quality.yml). `slotFixture` measures 11.2, which fails the `crap` check outright (see also the `fixture` regression comment — both must be fixed for the gate to go green):

```
NEW > 8  js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js::slotFixture: 11.2
```

The complexity lives in the inline label-mapping + state-conditional list body. Extracting the payload shaping into helpers drops it under the threshold, e.g.:

```javascript
function withLabelObjs(p) {
    return { number: p.number, labels: (p.labels || []).map(function (n) { return { name: n }; }),
             head: { sha: p.headSha }, merged_at: p.merged_at };
}
// github_list_prs: function (a) {
//     listCalls.push(a);
//     var src = ((a && a.state) || 'open') === 'merged' ? (mergedPrs || []) : openPrs;
//     return JSON.stringify(src.map(withLabelObjs));
// },
```

Verify with: instrument the tree (`nyc instrument`), run `ci/run_with_coverage.js`, then `crap4js . --coverage <cov> --threshold 8 --baseline crap-baseline.json` → expect `0 regression(s), 0 new over threshold`.

